le ordering. Enumerate all valid mappings after identity has failed, not merely one representative or one mapping per symmetry class. Restore reference output order by deriving each solution's exact recursive Heap-block ordering key and sorting by that key. Ordinary lexicographic permutation order and ordinary factorial-number-system permutation ranks are not Heap order. Use a mixed-radix digit vector or another overflow-safe representation; n! cannot be assumed to fit machine integers. Bound stored solutions and provide a correct streaming Heap-order fallback before emitting buffered results if storage becomes excessive. Compare the benefit of stronger search ordering against key-generation, sorting and setup costs; abandon this route if those costs dominate.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only independently correct, measured candidates. First establish exact output compatibility through the existing unmodified correctness mechanism, with explicit correctness reasoning for identity-isomorphic graphs, nonidentity mappings with multiple solutions, loops, repeated input edges, unequal sizes and nonisomorphic graphs sharing invariants. Review A's skipped-subtree exit state, B's mismatch-update accounting and C's Heap ordering especially carefully. Measure promising combinations separately: structural rejection plus cheap verification, ordered pruning plus buffering, and the alternative constraint solver. Do not assume gains compose; retain the best validated standalone candidate if integration regresses. Use the unchanged automatic timing procedure and existing budget, accounting for the approximately 10 ms baseline and its observed variation. Prefer serial execution absent evidence that parallel work offsets startup and ordered-output costs; any parallel candidate must respect four CPU cores and the existing build. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, target, permissions and budgets unchanged.\",\"analysis\":\"The target is Problem A's src/brute_isomorphism.cpp; roles B and C are research branches, not the other contest problems. The sole measured baseline passes four cases, averaging 0.0101544 s with samples from 0.0092865 to 0.0107938 s. No input sizes or profiling breakdown are supplied, so neither a dominant bottleneck nor a parallel speedup is established. After identity fails, the source performs factorial Heap enumeration with short-circuit adjacency checks and flushes each successful output line. The critical compatibility requirement is unusual: an identity isomorphism prints only identity and returns; otherwise the program prints every successful permutation in Heap order, or exactly 'The graphs are not isomorphic' if none succeeds. A conventional first-solution graph-isomorphism solver would therefore change observable behavior. Preserve diagonal self-loops, boolean deduplication of repeated edges, adjacency and non-adjacency, mapping direction, trailing spaces and newlines. Output volume itself can be factorial. The proposed branches balance asymptotic pruning, inexpensive implementation improvements and a more ambitious constrained search, without specializing to the four observed cases.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"nonce\":\"2cfdd06864064ccaaa4a945cba4bb9e6\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"c4e90ec0c6d2c6627813931f9823416814b629fdddbd6ac868da25f038026453\",\"session_id\":\"c0e9dfffccc040969abe9f6f54635671\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"c02b013b116091e239eca4f05d9d5d011839626ff3f391dbdb97822dcc22a0a9\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":11444,\"output_tokens\":6141,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":5178}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":17585,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
